James encountered an error (`/Users/admin/opt/anaconda3/bin/mpic++: line 282: -I/Users/admin/opt/anaconda3/include: No such file or directory`) when using `mpic++`. Despite confirming that the directory exists, the issue persisted since the `-I` flag was generated by `mpic++`. After investigating, it was found that no MPI-related environment variables were set. James then inquired about reinstalling `mpic++`, leading to the reinstallation of MPI via conda. After the reinstallation, a new error occurred: `Undefined symbols for architecture arm64`, specifically related to `MPI::ERRORS_THROW_EXCEPTIONS`. James shared the `mpic++ --show` output, revealing the use of Open MPI installed via Homebrew, indicating a need for correct linking flags and verifying compatibility.
